Z||000000||Fiero_RKM||04-19-2001||12:53 PM||||I have a very nice low-mile '88 Fromula that I was thinking of re-bodying into a GT.  Do you think this will wreck any future value it may have?  Should '88s generally be left stock?  I really like the GT cosmetically but I like the mechanicals and handling of my 88 much more than I did on my previous 86 GT.<P>Any thoughts would be welcome.<P>P.S.  Anybody know of a donor car with a decent rear clip (black a plus) in the upstate N.Y. area if I do decide to go ahead?<P>Regards....<BR>RKM||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-19-2001||12:57 PM||||I would keep it stock.  There aren't too many Formula's around anymore, especially lower mileage ones.  You can pick up 86/87 GT's cheap if you really want a fastback.  Notchbacks are cheaper to maintain too since they don't have expensive tail lights/Qtr. Windows.<P><BR>just my 2 cents...||||reg||3
Z||000002||sqoach||04-19-2001||12:58 PM||||No! Don't do it!!!<P>Hehe...well that's what I think.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||01:11 PM||||The fact that you are even considering a body change to an '88 Forumula indicates you are not worthy to own it.<P>The Fiero Preservation Police (FPP) unit from Rochester will be at your location in 45 minutes to place your vehicle into protective custody. Please remain sitting by your PC and dont move.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
