Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||02:44 PM||||Fairport is only 60 miles from Syracuse. You can park all the Fieros you want in my garage here, you just have to leave the keys here,<P>   and give me a days warning when you want to come use one so I can hook the odo back up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jaei Sun||04-19-2001||03:44 PM||||If I had the GT Pannels ready, I'd do it in a heart beat.  I've noticed on this board that everyone here things Formulas are the greatest fiero ever.  I think that they're just a coupe with a wing and what's the big deal with that?  Who cares if formulas are rare... you can always make one out of an 88 coupe, just drop a 2.8 in (why? just go to a 3.4) and add a wing... big whoop.<P>I don't understand the "keep it stock" guys, why???  Make it better than when it left the factory.  Put some different wheels on it...  I never liked the cross lace wheels... too plain looking, put some aftermarket wheels on!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Steve Normington||04-19-2001||03:54 PM||||Jaei Sun, those are some sweet rims you have on your signature. Where'd you get them and how much were they?<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 2M6||||reg||11
Z||000013||Black88GT||04-19-2001||04:04 PM||||No one here is saying Formula's are the greatest.  However, making one into a GT makes no sense.  Swapping the engine, OK.  New wheels, sure.  But changing it into a fastback is pointless since you can already buy a fastback easily and cheaply.  <P>With that being said, I believe Formula's are the best stock Fiero's though since they are lighter then '88 GT's and have all the mechanics/improvements of an '88 GT.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||05:19 PM||||whats the big deal with the wing?!<P>whats the big deal with the fake back seat windows?! The roof line of the car is still interupted by the vertical back window, so the GT body style is, i dont know what it is?! Its not an aerodynamic improvement as long as the rear window opening is still there...<P>I guess we should be glad they didnt put fake side windows down the front hood too.||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||04-19-2001||05:22 PM||||I've been thinking along similar lines. I would really like to find an '88GT and ditch the fastback clip and tailights and put notchback pieces in their place. I like my '86SE but the handling difference between my Formula and SE is huge. And since I don't want to change my baby(my Formula), and I love the aero-notchback. An '88GT converted to notchback is the ultimate Fiero, next to the Formula, if you ask me.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||04-19-2001||05:23 PM||||The big deal with the Formulas is that they are very distinctive looking. The GTs look like a lot of other cars, Mazdas, sorta like a camero/firebird...||||reg||1
Z||000017||Pontiaddict||04-19-2001||05:35 PM||||I will agree with what Black88GT and Fiero56 said. I like fastback GT's and SE's but I don't plan on making my 86GT into one. Why not use your Formula as a bargaining chip and find a GT, you get what you want, they get what they want, and you don't have to change all the body panels.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Galen||04-19-2001||08:39 PM||||lets put it this way, and if any of ya'll know me you know I hate stock cars, its your car.. you leave it stock, its still your car but its not YOUR car. Make it your own, give it a touch of personal style. If that means a fastback clip, then do it. I'd love to do my 88 into a fastback. Formulas are good, but its not gonna be good if you dont want it like that. And there are a bunch of Fiero's that can be made to look like formulas, atleast 20k of em.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Tom88gt||04-19-2001||09:38 PM||||I say go for it.  My car is an 88 Formula.  I want a GT (my screen name is a dream).  The style of the GT is more important than light weight of the Formula.  Yes, I could sell the 88 Formula and buy an 88 GT.  But My Formula is a T-top and T-tops are so rare that I can't find another T-top for less than several thousand$.  I won't even think about selling my Formula T-top for less than $5,000.  88 GTs are rare too so get an 86-87 GT for cheap and swap the panels.  That's my plan. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||gixxer||04-19-2001||09:56 PM||||It's YOUR car.<BR>Do what you want with it.||||reg||1
Z||000021||danny boy||04-20-2001||12:39 AM|||| I though t about changing my GT to a notchback when it gets painter simply because I haven't been able to find a taillight and those sail wondows are so expensive. I also very much like the look of the 85GT. Then it dawned on me.Why not take the 87 coupe I already have and put the right Fascias on it and theres my 85GT. Of course, the 85GT partscar helped out a bunch.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Spektyr||04-20-2001||02:09 AM||||How about a comprimise?<P>If you have a Formula, and you want to make it into a GT, do it.  Just keep all the old parts!<P>That way, it can always be turned back into a Formula, and the 'value' of the car is actually improved.<P>Example:  88 GT cloned from Formula for sale, still have all the Formula parts, all for X,XXX dollars.<P>The buyer would be anyone who likes the GT OR the Formula.<P>Even easier to do the switch back if the original color is maintained...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
Z||000023||Cameron||04-20-2001||03:22 AM||||My take on it is that it should be left stock, but if you have your heart set on some sort of change with it the most I would do is put the GT front fascia on it, but that is even a stretch.  I once owned an '88 Formula.  They are great, I wouldn't see why you would want to change the body.  If you want a GT buy a GT, but don't butcher a beautiful car.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||DaRkLoRD||04-20-2001||05:32 AM||||While you're at it, why not get a base model Civic and make it into a Civic Si? all you need is a bit of different trim, and the badges..<P>I have no problem with people changing their cars from stock, when I'm done, mine won't even say Fiero.. but pretending your car is something it's not (kitcars excepted....) it rice, plain and simple. if it's not a GT, saying it is a GT is a lie IMHO.<P>I don't get it why a bunch of you guys trash "ricers" for doing one thing, and when a fiero owner suggests the same thing, you say "go for it, it's your car"... true, a formula to a GT isn't the worst thing in the world. but I've seen more 88 coupes rebadged to be fake formulas than I care to remember..<P>anyway, to answer your question.. I say no.. modify it as much as you want, but saying it's something it's not.. isn;t an upgrade, it's a lie<P>(just my opinion.. heavily influenced by the fact that I'm in the middle of final exams, my final research report is already a day late and I'm not even 3/4 done yet, and I haven't slept in 2 days.)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
Z||000025||Jaei Sun||04-20-2001||11:09 AM||||"...whats the big deal with the fake back seat windows?!"<P>You could say the same about the MR2 MKii or the Delorean for that matter... and doesn't the Notchback have "Fake" windows too the sail panels?<P>"The big deal with the Formulas is that they are very distinctive looking"<P>-- They're just a coupe with a wing... there are more than 15k Fiero Coupes out there than any other body style fiero out there.<P>If you're just going for the LOOKS, you can achieve the same result by adding a wing to a coupe and there is your "distinctive" looking Fiero.<P>You're saying that fastbacks look like other cars well I can say the same about a Formula.  Hmmm Fiat X/9, Nissan Pulse, Honda Del Sol all look very similar.<P>I like Notchbacks but for me, they've got to have the GFX --- Indy, 85 GTs, and the later SEs.<P>"...why not get a base model Civic and make it into a Civic Si? All you need is a bit of different trim, and the badges."<P>That's completely different.  Those people that do that are trying to fool others into thinking that they have the 160+ HP VTEC motor.  Formulas and GTs are completely the same cept for the body panels.  It's not like you're putting a GT body on a 2.5 L coupe... that would be the proper comparison.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||qwikgta||04-21-2001||11:58 PM||||Want to see another "fake" Formula, go to my site (below), I still need to do the rear swaybar, and the engine swap but Im getting there, piece by piece.  <P>Go for it... Ive seen some pics of coupes with the GT clip. leave the coupe nose, rear bumper and no ground effects..it looks great. I'll do it when i find the parts.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
